\pard\plain \tx0\tx360\tx720\tx1080\tx1440\tx1800\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\sa360\sl264\slmult1\ltrch\loch {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 Revision mode allows you to use a different text colour while editing or revising your text, without having to change the colour again every time you click into a different part of a document.}
\par\pard\plain \tx0\tx360\tx720\tx1080\tx1440\tx1800\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\li763\fi-475\sa240\ql\ltrch\loch {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 <$Scr_Ps::0>\bullet \tab To enter revision mode, select one of the colours (\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8220\'93First Revision\u8221\'94, \u8220\'93Second Revision\u8221\'94 and so on) from the }{\f3\fs22\b1\i0\cf4 <$Scr_Cs::1>Format > Revision Mode<!$Scr_Cs::1>}{\f1\fs24\b0\i0  menu.}
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 \bullet \tab You can set your preferred revision colours in the \loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8220\'93Editing\u8221\'94 tab of the Options).}
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 \bullet \tab In revision mode, no matter where you click in the text, when you start typing the text will appear in the chosen revision colour.<!$Scr_Ps::0>}}